{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>To You</b> — Now he mentions the matter of the firmament and the dry land, for He desires to create man. And behold, the heavens are those near to the earth, and תבל is the inhabited part of the earth; therefore, 'and its fullness.'" "<b>And the meaning of You founded them</b> — a hint to the seven boundaries of all the inhabited world, and so they shall always be."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 89, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:36:27.576651897Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}